senses.gloss:
राजक॑ m. little king, also = राजन् (—˚);
 n. a
multitude of kings.

र॑जन f. ई colouring;
 m. ray, beam, N. of a man, f. ई
night.

र॑जस् n. atmosphere, air, esp. the lower region of clouds
and vapours (opp. दि॑व् or रा॑चन);
 the sky (conc. also as twofold,
रजसी) mist, gloom (i.g.);
 dust, pollen of flowers, any small
particle of matter;
 foulness, impurity, esp. the menstrual secretion,
darkness or soul-darkening passion (ph.).

रजस्वल a. dusty or full of passion;
 f. आ
menstruating, a woman during the menses.

राजकुल n. a king's or a royal family;
 the court of a
king.

राजगृह n. a king's house, palace;
 n. (& f. ई) N. of a
town.

राजधर्म m. a king's duty;
 Pl. the laws relating to
kings.

1 रा॑जन् m. king, ruler (often of gods, esp. of Soma), a man
of the military caste;
 f. रा॑ज्ञी queen.

राजन्य॑ a. royal, princely;
 m. a man of the military
caste;
 abstr. ˚त्व† n.

1 राजपुत्र॑ m. a king's son, prince (f. ˚पुत्री);
 a
Rājpoot.

राजराज m. = prec. (abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.);
 E. of
Kubera.

राजार्ह a. worthy of a king, royal, princely;
 n.
Agallochum.

राजीव a. striped;
 m. a cert. fish;
 n. a blue lotus-flower.

राज्य॑ a. fit to reign, royal;
 n. (also रा॑ज्य or
राज्य॑) kingship, sovereignty, reign, kingdom, country.
